    "finalAnswer": "# Diagnosis\n\n**Cause:** `CheckoutModel.totalCents` returns only the price of the *last* selected item instead of summing all selected items. With Bread ($3) and Apple ($2) selected, it returns $2 (Apple, the last added) rather than $5.\n\n**File / function responsible:** `examples/diagnostic-app/Sources/CheckoutModel.swift` — the computed property `CheckoutModel.totalCents`.\n\n**Smallest fix:** Replace the body of `totalCents` to sum prices instead of taking the last:\n\n```swift\nvar totalCents: Int {\n    selectedItems.reduce(0) { $0 + $1.priceCents }\n}\n```\n\nThis makes the confirmation display `Total: $5` (300 + 200), matching the claim. The observed line items (`Bread: $3`, `Apple: $2`) already render correctly from `ConfirmationView`, confirming the bug is isolated to the total calculation.",
